I implemented `format` in `format.ts`, keeping the export and signature. I only ran a quick spot check of a few conversions, not a full test suite. The private tests have not been run.

The spot check covered:
- the rounding examples from the README (`%.0f`, `%.2f` on 0.125 and 2.675);
- `%g` switching between `f` and `e` style;
- `%e`, `%G`, `%#o`, `%#x`, and the `0`, `-` and `+` flags;
- `%s` and `%c` with width and precision;
- a denormal (`5e-324`) and `1e21`.

All of those matched what the README describes. I did not try `Infinity`, `NaN`, bigint arguments, or `-0`.

It uses exact `BigInt` arithmetic on each double's binary value, so rounding is round-half-even on the true value. It uses no dependencies and does not shell out.

I left a scratch copy at `/tmp/f.ts` and a test script at `/tmp/t.ts`, both outside the workspace.
